WEBVTT

1
01:07:49.290 --> 01:07:52.290
Prophets and priests of these families will arise.

2
01:07:52.290 --> 01:07:57.290
In Jesus' name, Lord, I pray that you will raise up children of God from these families.

3
01:07:57.290 --> 01:08:00.290
They will walk in the shadow of the Most High God.

4
01:08:00.290 --> 01:08:06.290
Under the wing of protection of the Almighty, that these children will be protected.

5
01:08:06.290 --> 01:08:11.290
Lastly, I want to pray that our children growing up in an ideology of this world,

6
01:08:11.290 --> 01:08:17.290
that the parents will be equipped with the powerful truth of King Jesus.

7
01:08:17.290 --> 01:08:21.290
That when the children come home with teachings from their books,

8
01:08:21.290 --> 01:08:25.290
they will know, look, this is what the school says, but this is what God's Word says.

9
01:08:25.290 --> 01:08:30.290
And even though we have respect for the schools, we have respect for the authorities,

10
01:08:30.290 --> 01:08:33.290
we have respect for the places in which we live.

11
01:08:33.290 --> 01:08:37.290
Paul says, pray also for the government. So we are not enemies of the government,

12
01:08:37.290 --> 01:08:40.290
but we have respect for the government and we pray for it.

13
01:08:40.290 --> 01:08:44.290
But when our children learn things from the schools,

14
01:08:44.290 --> 01:08:48.290
what is not normative, what God's Word says, is normative for the children.

15
01:08:48.290 --> 01:08:51.290
And I bless you parents in the name of Jesus,

16
01:08:51.290 --> 01:08:54.290
that you will receive supernatural wisdom,

17
01:08:54.290 --> 01:09:00.290
to present God's Word in a healthy contrast in the family in which you live.

18
01:09:00.290 --> 01:09:03.290
And the words of Joshua resonate strongly here.

19
01:09:03.290 --> 01:09:09.290
But as for me and my house, we will serve the Lord. Amen?

20
01:09:09.290 --> 01:09:12.290
Amen, amen, amen.

21
01:09:12.290 --> 01:09:14.290
Super.

22
01:09:14.290 --> 01:09:16.290
Thank you all very much.

23
01:09:16.290 --> 01:09:20.290
I would like to move you to the right side of the stage.

24
01:09:20.290 --> 01:09:32.290
You will get a Playstation or something, a game console, a skateboard, a fatbike.

25
01:09:35.290 --> 01:09:38.290
Fatbikes are prohibited.

26
01:09:38.290 --> 01:09:42.290
Right? Hopefully no one in this church has a fatbike, right?

27
01:09:42.290 --> 01:09:45.290
No? Good, good people.

28
01:09:45.290 --> 01:09:47.290
ASO-bikes.

29
01:09:47.290 --> 01:09:50.290
Prize in the name of Jesus. Hallelujah.

30
01:09:50.290 --> 01:09:54.290
But isn't it nice for the church to be a congregation, huh?

31
01:09:54.290 --> 01:09:56.290
Isn't that nice people?

32
01:09:56.290 --> 01:09:58.290
I love it.

33
01:09:58.290 --> 01:10:00.290
Hello.

34
01:10:02.290 --> 01:10:04.290
Hallelujah.

35
01:10:05.290 --> 01:10:09.290
Robert, may I invite you to the stage?

36
01:10:22.290 --> 01:10:27.290
Yes, I want to talk to you this morning about Jacob.

37
01:10:28.290 --> 01:10:39.290
Jacob had quite taken advantage of his brother by tricking him out of his birthright.

38
01:10:39.290 --> 01:10:48.290
And by stealing or deceiving the blessing from his father Isaac.

39
01:10:48.290 --> 01:10:51.290
He had pretended to be Esau.

40
01:10:51.290 --> 01:10:55.290
And Esau was of course very angry with Jacob.

41
01:10:56.290 --> 01:10:58.290
And they wanted to kill him.

42
01:10:58.290 --> 01:11:02.290
And Jacob then goes on the run.

43
01:11:02.290 --> 01:11:05.290
For yes, he thinks this is going completely wrong here.

44
01:11:05.290 --> 01:11:09.290
And he decides to flee far away to an uncle of theirs.

45
01:11:09.290 --> 01:11:11.290
His name was Laban.

46
01:11:11.290 --> 01:11:14.290
And there he is then.

47
01:11:14.290 --> 01:11:18.290
He had grown up in a beautiful family, full of God's blessing.

48
01:11:18.290 --> 01:11:22.290
And there he is then, on the road all alone.

49
01:11:22.290 --> 01:11:27.290
And in the desert, having left everything behind.

50
01:11:27.290 --> 01:11:30.290
And then he has a dream.

51
01:11:30.290 --> 01:11:33.290
And in that dream, he sees angels.

52
01:11:33.290 --> 01:11:37.290
He sees a ladder going from the earth all the way to heaven.

53
01:11:37.290 --> 01:11:44.290
And he sees how angels go up and down over that ladder.

54
01:11:44.290 --> 01:11:47.290
And that is an image of an open heaven.

55
01:11:47.290 --> 01:11:52.290
That angels can freely ascend and descend from God's throne to the earth.

56
01:11:52.290 --> 01:11:56.290
And we always pray at a quarter to ten.

57
01:11:56.290 --> 01:11:59.290
Every Sunday morning before the service begins together.

58
01:11:59.290 --> 01:12:04.290
And you are warmly welcome to join in.

59
01:12:04.290 --> 01:12:06.290
For that is always very valuable.

60
01:12:06.290 --> 01:12:09.290
And you have a good place to park your car.

61
01:12:09.290 --> 01:12:14.290
So double reason to be here at a quarter to ten.

62
01:12:14.290 --> 01:12:17.290
But Vanessa mentioned praying.

63
01:12:17.290 --> 01:12:22.290
She began to pray for an open heaven in our church.

64
01:12:22.290 --> 01:12:26.290
That it is easy to meet God from this place.

65
01:12:26.290 --> 01:12:32.290
And then at the end she also spoke about angels working in our midst.

66
01:12:32.290 --> 01:12:35.290
And we did not know it about each other.

67
01:12:35.290 --> 01:12:38.290
But that is exactly the same as that ladder Jacob saw.

68
01:12:38.290 --> 01:12:41.290
So Father thank you Lord that you speak.

69
01:12:41.290 --> 01:12:47.290
Thank you that you want to make Open Church a place where it is easy to meet you.

70
01:12:47.290 --> 01:12:52.290
Help us Lord as a whole church to have an open heaven in our midst.

71
01:12:52.290 --> 01:12:56.290
Help us Lord with everything that stands between you and us.

72
01:12:56.290 --> 01:13:01.290
Every blockage, every sin, every unwillingness, and so on.

73
01:13:02.290 --> 01:13:04.290
Help us Lord to remove it.

74
01:13:04.290 --> 01:13:11.290
So that we have an open way, a closeness to you and knowing you.

75
01:13:11.290 --> 01:13:13.290
Hallelujah.

76
01:13:13.290 --> 01:13:17.290
We are going to read in the Bible.

77
01:13:18.290 --> 01:13:23.290
At the top of the ladder he saw the Lord standing, Jacob that is.

78
01:13:23.290 --> 01:13:26.290
The Lord said to Jacob.

79
01:13:26.290 --> 01:13:32.290
I am the Lord, the God of your grandfather Abraham and the God of your father Isaac.

80
01:13:32.290 --> 01:13:38.290
The land where you now lie I will give to you, to your family, after you.

81
01:13:38.290 --> 01:13:42.290
Your family will be as countless as the dust of the earth.

82
01:13:42.290 --> 01:13:46.290
They will spread to the west, east, north, and south.

83
01:13:46.290 --> 01:13:54.290
And through the blessing that is upon you and your son, all the people of the earth will be blessed.

84
01:13:54.290 --> 01:13:58.290
I am with you and I will protect you wherever you go.

85
01:13:58.290 --> 01:14:01.290
And I will bring you back to this land.

86
01:14:01.290 --> 01:14:05.290
For I will not leave you, but will do what I have said to you.

87
01:14:05.290 --> 01:14:13.290
This says God about Jacob and his descendants, the people of Israel.

88
01:14:14.290 --> 01:14:20.290
And God says here, this land is yours Israel.

89
01:14:20.290 --> 01:14:24.290
And God even says, in this the whole earth will be blessed.

90
01:14:24.290 --> 01:14:30.290
Well, whatever has happened in Israel now in our time.

91
01:14:30.290 --> 01:14:33.290
We do not engage in politics, we engage in the Bible.

92
01:14:33.290 --> 01:14:37.290
The Bible says, God has given the Israelites this land.

93
01:14:37.290 --> 01:14:42.290
And if we bless Israel, we will be blessed in them.

94
01:14:42.290 --> 01:14:46.290
That is the promise that God gives here and in many other places.

95
01:14:46.290 --> 01:14:50.290
So let us take a moment to bless Israel.

96
01:14:50.290 --> 01:14:56.290
Thank you Lord, for this people Lord, for the descendants of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.

97
01:14:56.290 --> 01:15:01.290
Bless your people Lord, help them Lord to find you.

98
01:15:01.290 --> 01:15:03.290
That they may see their Messiah.

99
01:15:03.290 --> 01:15:05.290
That they will begin to follow him.

100
01:15:05.290 --> 01:15:07.290
And that it will go well with them.

101
01:15:07.290 --> 01:15:10.290
And that they will be able to live in the knowledge of You.

102
01:15:10.290 --> 01:15:14.290
And in peace in the land that You have destined for them.

103
01:15:14.290 --> 01:15:16.290
Hallelujah.

104
01:15:20.290 --> 01:15:25.290
Then Jacob naturally responds to what he hears God saying in that dream.

105
01:15:25.290 --> 01:15:30.290
Jacob promised, if God indeed takes care of me.

106
01:15:30.290 --> 01:15:32.290
Will protect me on a journey.

107
01:15:32.290 --> 01:15:35.290
Will provide enough food and clothes to wear.

108
01:15:35.290 --> 01:15:40.290
And if I return safely to my family, then the Lord my God will be.

109
01:15:40.290 --> 01:15:45.290
And this stone that I have set up as a pillar will be a house of God.

110
01:15:45.290 --> 01:15:52.290
And I promise that I will give Him a tenth of everything He gives me.

111
01:15:54.290 --> 01:15:57.290
Jacob makes a covenant with God here.

112
01:15:57.290 --> 01:16:03.290
Yes, if this is my God, if He loves me, if He wants to bless me.

113
01:16:03.290 --> 01:16:07.290
Then I will give Him 10% of all my income.

114
01:16:07.290 --> 01:16:09.290
Of everything He provides for me.

115
01:16:09.290 --> 01:16:12.290
Not because I have to, but because I love Him.

116
01:16:12.290 --> 01:16:15.290
Because I want to enter into covenant with Him.

117
01:16:18.290 --> 01:16:22.290
Laban, then he goes on to Laban.

118
01:16:22.290 --> 01:16:25.290
He arrives at his uncle's place.

119
01:16:25.290 --> 01:16:28.290
And there turns out to be a gigantic swindler.

120
01:16:32.290 --> 01:16:35.290
Laban has two daughters, Rachel.

121
01:16:35.290 --> 01:16:38.290
He falls head over heels in love with her, he wants to marry her.

122
01:16:38.290 --> 01:16:45.290
He says, Laban that's fine, but then you have to work for me for 7 years as a sort of bride price.

123
01:16:45.290 --> 01:16:48.290
Well, he loves Rachel so much that he does it.

124
01:16:48.290 --> 01:16:53.290
He works for 7 years and then they are going to marry, and then Laban pulls a trick.

125
01:16:53.290 --> 01:16:58.290
Which causes him to spend the wedding night with Leah instead of Rachel.

126
01:16:58.290 --> 01:17:01.290
Then he is stuck with Leah, which he does not want at all.

127
01:17:01.290 --> 01:17:03.290
He still wants Rachel.

128
01:17:03.290 --> 01:17:09.290
And then Laban says, the deceiver is good, you may work for me for another 7 years as a bride price.

129
01:17:09.290 --> 01:17:11.290
You may marry her.

130
01:17:11.290 --> 01:17:15.290
Jacob does that, because he loves her so much.

131
01:17:15.290 --> 01:17:23.290
Then, after 14 years, he is finally married to Rachel as well.

132
01:17:23.290 --> 01:17:28.290
And then he says, now I would like to start building my own wealth.

133
01:17:28.290 --> 01:17:32.290
Because I have gathered so much wealth for you, Laban.

134
01:17:32.290 --> 01:17:34.290
Let me work now.

135
01:17:34.290 --> 01:17:39.290
And you know what, of all the bucks and goats and sheep.

136
01:17:39.290 --> 01:17:45.290
Let all the spotted and striped lambs that are born be mine.

137
01:17:45.290 --> 01:17:51.290
And all those that are solid colored, brown or white, they are for Laban.

138
01:17:51.290 --> 01:17:53.290
That's fine, says Laban.

139
01:17:53.290 --> 01:17:55.290
What does Laban do then?

140
01:17:55.290 --> 01:18:04.290
He takes away all the spotted and speckled adult animals and all the brown animals from the flock.

141
01:18:04.290 --> 01:18:10.290
And he brings them at a distance of three days, so that they certainly cannot cross with the others.

142
01:18:10.290 --> 01:18:14.290
And what does Jacob do then?

143
01:18:14.290 --> 01:18:18.290
He takes doubts, he alters them so that there are stripes on those doubts.

144
01:18:18.290 --> 01:18:22.290
And he throws them into the drinking trough when the strong animals are going to mate.

145
01:18:22.290 --> 01:18:32.290
And what happens? Because God blesses, many strong, good, striped and spotted little animals are born.

146
01:18:32.290 --> 01:18:36.290
And so Jacob becomes very rich.

147
01:18:36.290 --> 01:18:38.290
God blesses him.

148
01:18:38.290 --> 01:18:41.290
Eventually, he is going to leave Laban.

149
01:18:41.290 --> 01:18:45.290
And then he meets God again on the way.

150
01:18:45.290 --> 01:18:48.290
And then he says the following to God.

151
01:18:53.290 --> 01:18:57.290
I have the wrong text here.

152
01:18:57.290 --> 01:19:00.290
Do you have Genesis 32 verse 10?

153
01:19:11.290 --> 01:19:14.290
Genesis 32 verse 10.

154
01:19:15.290 --> 01:19:18.290
Then Jacob says.

155
01:19:18.290 --> 01:19:23.290
I am not worthy at all that you have been so good to me.

156
01:19:23.290 --> 01:19:26.290
And that you have given me so much.

157
01:19:26.290 --> 01:19:31.290
I had only a staff when I crossed the Jordan on my way here.

158
01:19:31.290 --> 01:19:37.290
Now I have these two large groups of people and animals.

159
01:19:38.290 --> 01:19:42.290
God has greatly blessed Jacob.

160
01:19:42.290 --> 01:19:44.290
Through everything.

161
01:19:44.290 --> 01:19:46.290
That is typical of God.

162
01:19:46.290 --> 01:19:50.290
It is not always that God lets everything go easily for us.

163
01:19:50.290 --> 01:19:52.290
But He does bless us.

164
01:19:52.290 --> 01:19:54.290
He ensures that things go well for us.

165
01:19:54.290 --> 01:19:56.290
And then whatever happens can happen.

166
01:19:56.290 --> 01:19:58.290
People can be for you or against you.

167
01:19:58.290 --> 01:20:00.290
You try to obstruct.

168
01:20:00.290 --> 01:20:03.290
You try to uplift as Laban did.

169
01:20:03.290 --> 01:20:06.290
But God always blesses above that.

170
01:20:06.290 --> 01:20:10.290
If you are faithful to God, God is faithful to you.

171
01:20:14.290 --> 01:20:18.290
Jacob therefore gave 10% of everything he received.

172
01:20:18.290 --> 01:20:21.290
Not because it had to be, but because he loves God.

173
01:20:21.290 --> 01:20:24.290
Because he made a covenant with Him.

174
01:20:24.290 --> 01:20:26.290
And this was before the law.

175
01:20:26.290 --> 01:20:30.290
Later in the law, which the people of God had.

176
01:20:30.290 --> 01:20:36.290
In the law that the people of God received through Moses.

177
01:20:36.290 --> 01:20:38.290
Then it becomes mandatory.

178
01:20:38.290 --> 01:20:40.290
God's principle is then.

179
01:20:40.290 --> 01:20:44.290
All Israelites must give 10% of their income.

180
01:20:44.290 --> 01:20:49.290
So that the priests, the Levites, are exempt.

181
01:20:49.290 --> 01:20:52.290
And that they do not have to work for their income.

182
01:20:52.290 --> 01:20:54.290
But that they can fully focus on God.

183
01:20:54.290 --> 01:20:57.290
Now we are no longer under the law.

184
01:20:57.290 --> 01:20:59.290
For in Jesus we are free.

185
01:20:59.290 --> 01:21:02.290
But the purpose of the law still stands.

186
01:21:02.290 --> 01:21:07.290
How great is it when we continue with this principle of God.

187
01:21:07.290 --> 01:21:09.290
By being generous.

188
01:21:09.290 --> 01:21:11.290
By bringing our tithe back to Him.

189
01:21:11.290 --> 01:21:13.290
That we have a building here.

190
01:21:13.290 --> 01:21:15.290
That we can establish a larger building.

191
01:21:15.290 --> 01:21:18.290
That we can pay pastors.

192
01:21:18.290 --> 01:21:21.290
So that they can fully focus on God the whole week.

193
01:21:21.290 --> 01:21:23.290
And build this church.

194
01:21:23.290 --> 01:21:26.290
That is God's principle of the tithe.

195
01:21:26.290 --> 01:21:35.290
I speak about this quite difficultly.

196
01:21:35.290 --> 01:21:37.290
And every week we talk about giving.

197
01:21:37.290 --> 01:21:40.290
And we do that very consciously.

198
01:21:40.290 --> 01:21:42.290
And sometimes we receive criticism for it.

199
01:21:42.290 --> 01:21:44.290
But this is important.

200
01:21:44.290 --> 01:21:46.290
Do you know why?

201
01:21:46.290 --> 01:21:49.290
First of all, when you give, God is blessed.

202
01:21:49.290 --> 01:21:52.290
When you give out of love.

203
01:21:52.290 --> 01:21:54.290
Then that is the covenant with Him.

204
01:21:54.290 --> 01:21:56.290
That love relationship is so great.

205
01:21:56.290 --> 01:21:58.290
God finds that so pleasing.

206
01:21:58.290 --> 01:22:01.290
When you show in your giving that you trust Him.

207
01:22:01.290 --> 01:22:03.290
And you are also blessed.

208
01:22:03.290 --> 01:22:06.290
That is the promise that God gives.

209
01:22:06.290 --> 01:22:09.290
And God's kingdom is being built.

210
01:22:09.290 --> 01:22:11.290
And that is also super important.

211
01:22:11.290 --> 01:22:14.290
It is important that we have a good building.

212
01:22:14.290 --> 01:22:19.290
It is important that our pastors can be full-time engaged with God.

213
01:22:19.290 --> 01:22:23.290
So therefore be generous.

214
01:22:23.290 --> 01:22:25.290
Invest your money for Him.

215
01:22:25.290 --> 01:22:27.290
Trust in God.

216
01:22:27.290 --> 01:22:30.290
Enter into the covenant with Him.

217
01:22:30.290 --> 01:22:32.290
Do not be afraid.

218
01:22:32.290 --> 01:22:34.290
How will it go if I give away my money?

219
01:22:34.290 --> 01:22:36.290
Then I will fall short.

220
01:22:36.290 --> 01:22:37.290
Trust in God.

221
01:22:37.290 --> 01:22:39.290
He will always bless you.

222
01:22:39.290 --> 01:22:58.290
Are we ready for God's Word?

223
01:22:58.290 --> 01:23:00.290
Anyone?

224
01:23:01.290 --> 01:23:03.290
Are we ready for God's Word?

225
01:23:03.290 --> 01:23:06.290
Anyone?

226
01:23:06.290 --> 01:23:09.290
Bram, you are very sweet.

227
01:23:09.290 --> 01:23:11.290
Announcement.

228
01:23:11.290 --> 01:23:14.290
Good letters written down.

229
01:23:14.290 --> 01:23:19.290
Next week we have a nice update.

230
01:23:19.290 --> 01:23:22.290
Here in the service about the construction project.

231
01:23:22.290 --> 01:23:25.290
There are good developments ahead.

232
01:23:25.290 --> 01:23:27.290
We are making good progress.

233
01:23:27.290 --> 01:23:32.290
The last time we gave an update here about the new construction project.

234
01:23:32.290 --> 01:23:34.290
Then we were very happy.

235
01:23:34.290 --> 01:23:40.290
By saying that we are not getting a loan from any bank.

236
01:23:40.290 --> 01:23:42.290
Regarding the new construction project.

237
01:23:42.290 --> 01:23:45.290
And we were like, praise the Lord.

238
01:23:45.290 --> 01:23:48.290
But of course we have worked very hard.

239
01:23:48.290 --> 01:23:51.290
We are talking with many people and parties.

240
01:23:51.290 --> 01:23:55.290
How can we work together as a church.

241
01:23:56.290 --> 01:23:59.290
In the name of Jesus, we are going to build this new building.

242
01:23:59.290 --> 01:24:01.290
I believe that it will happen.

243
01:24:01.290 --> 01:24:04.290
For I believe 100% for sure.

244
01:24:04.290 --> 01:24:07.290
That God has given us this task.

245
01:24:07.290 --> 01:24:10.290
After He gave us this task.

246
01:24:10.290 --> 01:24:12.290
We started to pray and said.

247
01:24:12.290 --> 01:24:15.290
Lord, if you truly speak in this.

248
01:24:15.290 --> 01:24:18.290
If this is your voice and not our own desires.

249
01:24:18.290 --> 01:24:20.290
Without our own impulsive ideas.

250
01:24:20.290 --> 01:24:23.290
If it is your intention for us to build a new building.

251
01:24:23.290 --> 01:24:26.290
God has then opened several doors.

