323
01:28:15.290 --> 01:28:19.290
And we draw out the lessons that we can learn from them.

324
01:28:19.290 --> 01:28:21.290
Therefore today Philippians chapter 3.

325
01:28:24.290 --> 01:28:26.290
What Paul is doing here.

326
01:28:28.290 --> 01:28:30.290
In this chapter.

327
01:28:30.290 --> 01:28:35.290
Is something that I often think about as well.

328
01:28:36.290 --> 01:28:43.290
A consideration of how you can talk to someone about a certain topic.

329
01:28:43.290 --> 01:28:45.290
Either to warn someone.

330
01:28:45.290 --> 01:28:49.290
Or to encourage someone in a piece of peace.

331
01:28:51.290 --> 01:28:54.290
Some time ago I had a conversation with my friend Bram.

332
01:28:54.290 --> 01:28:56.290
Who is sitting here.

333
01:28:56.290 --> 01:28:59.290
He is also the treasurer of open church.

334
01:29:00.290 --> 01:29:06.290
And Bram and Els lead a very stable life when it comes to their finances.

335
01:29:06.290 --> 01:29:09.290
They are good, as we say, stewards.

336
01:29:09.290 --> 01:29:13.290
When it comes to how to handle money.

337
01:29:13.290 --> 01:29:15.290
The Lord provides.

338
01:29:15.290 --> 01:29:18.290
And all the money we receive. Our jobs.

339
01:29:18.290 --> 01:29:21.290
The harvest we bring in comes from Him.

340
01:29:21.290 --> 01:29:25.290
A believer knows that everything comes from Him. Amen?

341
01:29:25.290 --> 01:29:32.290
So we on this earth receive a task as stewards for our lives.

342
01:29:32.290 --> 01:29:35.290
Or when you are independent.

343
01:29:35.290 --> 01:29:38.290
And everything that comes to you through your toil.

344
01:29:38.290 --> 01:29:42.290
You may distribute that as a steward on this earth.

345
01:29:42.290 --> 01:29:44.290
And you may live with that.

346
01:29:44.290 --> 01:29:46.290
You may be blessed with that.

347
01:29:46.290 --> 01:29:48.290
But all that provision comes from the Father.

348
01:29:48.290 --> 01:29:51.290
And some time ago I had a conversation with Bram.

349
01:29:51.290 --> 01:29:53.290
And we were just talking.

350
01:29:53.290 --> 01:29:55.290
And we were talking, for example, about...

351
01:29:55.290 --> 01:29:58.290
Bram, I don't know if you still remember that conversation.

352
01:29:58.290 --> 01:30:01.290
But we were talking, for example, about that when an entrepreneur...

353
01:30:01.290 --> 01:30:04.290
needs to borrow some money from the bank at a certain moment...

354
01:30:04.290 --> 01:30:08.290
to buy a work van.

355
01:30:08.290 --> 01:30:13.290
Then Bram said, well, a loan is actually not something the Bible is against at all.

356
01:30:13.290 --> 01:30:16.290
A loan is actually not sinful at all.

357
01:30:16.290 --> 01:30:20.290
It's fine to take out a loan in your life.

358
01:30:21.290 --> 01:30:25.290
And most people here in the room have a loan on their house, for example.

359
01:30:25.290 --> 01:30:27.290
A mortgage.

360
01:30:27.290 --> 01:30:30.290
Some people rent, and some people borrow money for a mortgage.

361
01:30:30.290 --> 01:30:33.290
Very few people buy a house cash.

362
01:30:33.290 --> 01:30:36.290
I am still praying for that.

363
01:30:36.290 --> 01:30:38.290
LAUGHTER

364
01:30:38.290 --> 01:30:41.290
But a mortgage is not bad at all.

365
01:30:41.290 --> 01:30:44.290
And also if you need a work van.

366
01:30:44.290 --> 01:30:48.290
You can choose to buy an old Ford Transit with 500,000 kilometers on the clock.

367
01:30:48.290 --> 01:30:52.290
Or you buy a new van and you buy it, for example, on installment.

368
01:30:52.290 --> 01:30:54.290
There is basically nothing wrong with that.

369
01:30:54.290 --> 01:30:57.290
The Bible has no problem with that.

370
01:30:57.290 --> 01:31:00.290
Being debt-free is wonderful.

371
01:31:00.290 --> 01:31:03.290
That is really nice and it is also an encouragement for guys...

372
01:31:03.290 --> 01:31:06.290
don't go borrowing everything at the cliffs.

373
01:31:06.290 --> 01:31:08.290
Yes, I want to go to that country once.

374
01:31:08.290 --> 01:31:11.290
You know what, I’ll go to the bank, I can take out a loan to go to Hawaii once.

375
01:31:11.290 --> 01:31:13.290
That is a stupid loan.

376
01:31:13.290 --> 01:31:15.290
Vacation loan, stupid loan.

377
01:31:15.290 --> 01:31:17.290
Work van loan, fine loan.

378
01:31:17.290 --> 01:31:20.290
As long as you handle it well.

379
01:31:20.290 --> 01:31:22.290
And when Bram said that...

380
01:31:22.290 --> 01:31:25.290
Then I replied to him, I said yes...

381
01:31:25.290 --> 01:31:32.290
but you have to be careful about who you say what to.

382
01:31:32.290 --> 01:31:35.290
Because namely, when Bram says...

383
01:31:35.290 --> 01:31:38.290
you can very well take out a loan...

384
01:31:38.290 --> 01:31:42.290
then Bram means that from his stability...

385
01:31:42.290 --> 01:31:46.290
and his wisdom and his life experience...

386
01:31:46.290 --> 01:31:49.290
by saying, if I handle this loan in my Excel sheet...

387
01:31:49.290 --> 01:31:51.290
Bram is an Excel sheet fan.

388
01:31:51.290 --> 01:31:55.290
If I manage this loan in my Excel sheet like this...

389
01:31:55.290 --> 01:31:58.290
then I can pay it off this way.

390
01:31:58.290 --> 01:32:01.290
Moreover, you even have a savings account with money for that.

391
01:32:01.290 --> 01:32:03.290
It can all be done.

392
01:32:03.290 --> 01:32:05.290
But he thinks through his wisdom...

393
01:32:05.290 --> 01:32:09.290
and he says, it's just a good business deal...

394
01:32:09.290 --> 01:32:11.290
to take out a loan.

395
01:32:11.290 --> 01:32:15.290
But, you better not say this to someone...

396
01:32:15.290 --> 01:32:17.290
who has two holes in his hands...

397
01:32:17.290 --> 01:32:19.290
and I'm not talking about the Lord Jesus...

398
01:32:19.290 --> 01:32:23.290
but I'm talking about someone who has two holes in his hands...

399
01:32:23.290 --> 01:32:25.290
from spending too much.

400
01:32:25.290 --> 01:32:29.290
People who just spend everything together.

401
01:32:29.290 --> 01:32:33.290
Never save, handle money very unreasonably...

402
01:32:33.290 --> 01:32:36.290
and so hop, money goes here and money goes there...

403
01:32:36.290 --> 01:32:38.290
and a new phone is coming out.

404
01:32:38.290 --> 01:32:40.290
I need to have it right away.

405
01:32:40.290 --> 01:32:42.290
Hey, but your phone is only a year old.

406
01:32:42.290 --> 01:32:44.290
Yes, but I want the newest one.

407
01:32:44.290 --> 01:32:47.290
Those people borrow everything from each other.

408
01:32:47.290 --> 01:32:50.290
In America, I sometimes hear that the average American...

409
01:32:50.290 --> 01:32:53.290
has about four credit cards.

410
01:32:53.290 --> 01:32:55.290
Be normal.

411
01:32:55.290 --> 01:32:57.290
And there is an 8 to 10% interest on that.

412
01:32:57.290 --> 01:33:00.290
You know, just borrowing, and borrowing, and borrowing.

413
01:33:00.290 --> 01:33:04.290
And so, at that moment it is unwise...

414
01:33:04.290 --> 01:33:07.290
even if Bram would say to that person...

415
01:33:07.290 --> 01:33:09.290
taking out a loan is fine.

416
01:33:09.290 --> 01:33:12.290
Because what that person receives in their soul...

417
01:33:12.290 --> 01:33:16.290
