431
01:33:52.290 --> 01:33:55.290
Because some people who are already overweight...

432
01:33:55.290 --> 01:33:57.290
and who are unhealthy...

433
01:33:57.290 --> 01:33:59.290
and who are on the brink of diabetes...

434
01:33:59.290 --> 01:34:01.290
or who have physical problems...

435
01:34:01.290 --> 01:34:03.290
and come to Joop with their overweight...

436
01:34:03.290 --> 01:34:06.290
if Joop then says, you can certainly eat a cake...

437
01:34:06.290 --> 01:34:08.290
you can certainly eat an apple turnover...

438
01:34:08.290 --> 01:34:10.290
you can certainly eat a bokkenpoot...

439
01:34:10.290 --> 01:34:12.290
bokkenpoots, do those still exist?

440
01:34:12.290 --> 01:34:15.290
you can certainly have a cream for you Belgians...

441
01:34:15.290 --> 01:34:18.290
then you have to be careful what you say about that.

442
01:34:18.290 --> 01:34:22.290
Because in the ears of the person it comes across as...

443
01:34:22.290 --> 01:34:26.290
ah, he says himself, I can just eat cookies.

444
01:34:26.290 --> 01:34:31.290
You have to be careful who you say what to.

445
01:34:31.290 --> 01:34:34.290
Because the person who receives us...

446
01:34:34.290 --> 01:34:36.290
has to receive something...

447
01:34:36.290 --> 01:34:42.290
to then place themselves correctly in a kind of discipline...

448
01:34:42.290 --> 01:34:45.290
of listen, I better not borrow money for this...

449
01:34:45.290 --> 01:34:48.290
and I better not borrow money for that and that and that...

450
01:34:48.290 --> 01:34:51.290
because I wouldn't be able to handle that...

451
01:34:51.290 --> 01:34:55.290
so that's why I have to place myself under a kind of discipline...

452
01:34:55.290 --> 01:34:57.290
by not doing something...

453
01:34:57.290 --> 01:34:59.290
