504
01:37:45.290 --> 01:37:49.290
And some of you then, who are sitting in the hall...

505
01:37:49.290 --> 01:37:53.290
and some of you are already living righteously.

506
01:37:53.290 --> 01:37:58.290
You have already been baptized in the Word, you no longer sin.

507
01:37:58.290 --> 01:38:02.290
Tim, here we go again with that humility.

508
01:38:02.290 --> 01:38:06.290
But Tim, no one can be perfect.

509
01:38:06.290 --> 01:38:10.290
But you can live righteously.

510
01:38:10.290 --> 01:38:13.290
And that must be the goal, we will read that shortly...

511
01:38:13.290 --> 01:38:15.290
in Philippians chapter 3.

512
01:38:15.290 --> 01:38:18.290
And some of us, when I call from a podium...

513
01:38:18.290 --> 01:38:21.290
guys, we must live more holily.

514
01:38:21.290 --> 01:38:24.290
Some of you, who are already living holy...

515
01:38:24.290 --> 01:38:29.290
receive that as a warning to live even holier.

516
01:38:29.290 --> 01:38:32.290
And then a danger arises...

517
01:38:32.290 --> 01:38:36.290
that such a person becomes completely obsessed with themselves...

518
01:38:36.290 --> 01:38:38.290
to try even harder to do better.

519
01:38:38.290 --> 01:38:41.290
Serve harder, give more.

520
01:38:41.290 --> 01:38:44.290
Come more often, do more, do more.

521
01:38:44.290 --> 01:38:49.290
Tim who said on Sunday, do more, do more, do more.

522
01:38:49.290 --> 01:38:52.290
Then you need the Holy Spirit who encourages you.

523
01:38:52.290 --> 01:38:56.290
Rest, for Jesus loves you.

524
01:38:56.290 --> 01:38:59.290
Rest, for Jesus loves you.

525
01:38:59.290 --> 01:39:03.290
Sometimes people from other churches come to this church...

526
01:39:03.290 --> 01:39:06.290
and then I notice that they have served themselves to exhaustion.

527
01:39:06.290 --> 01:39:09.290
That they have over-served themselves in life.

528
01:39:09.290 --> 01:39:11.290
Through ministries they have become tired.

529
01:39:11.290 --> 01:39:13.290
And then they come to an open church...

530
01:39:13.290 --> 01:39:16.290
and sometimes they come to me and say...

531
01:39:16.290 --> 01:39:18.290
What can I do here?

532
01:39:18.290 --> 01:39:21.290
And do you know what I often say? Come to rest.

533
01:39:21.290 --> 01:39:23.290
Just sit down comfortably.

534
01:39:23.290 --> 01:39:26.290
Receive God's Word, for that is the highest goal.

535
01:39:26.290 --> 01:39:28.290
To receive God. Come to rest.

536
01:39:28.290 --> 01:39:31.290
Chill out, for Jesus loves you.

537
01:39:31.290 --> 01:39:33.290
You can't add anything to it.

538
01:39:33.290 --> 01:39:36.290
You can't add anything to Him. He is who He is.

539
01:39:36.290 --> 01:39:39.290
He is so beautiful. He is so loving. He is so good.

540
01:39:39.290 --> 01:39:42.290
He is so gracious. He is so patient.

541
01:39:42.290 --> 01:39:45.290
He is awesome. His name is Jesus.

542
01:39:46.290 --> 01:39:49.290
Unfortunately, there is one problem with stubbornness...

543
01:39:49.290 --> 01:39:52.290
that we talked about last week...

544
01:39:52.290 --> 01:39:55.290
when we talk about humility versus stubbornness.

545
01:39:55.290 --> 01:39:58.290
Unfortunately, there is one problem that often exists in the churches...

546
01:39:58.290 --> 01:40:01.290
and church leaders are aware of this problem.

547
01:40:01.290 --> 01:40:05.290
That is when you jump on stage and say to the congregation...

548
01:40:05.290 --> 01:40:08.290
People, you need to start living righteously.

549
01:40:08.290 --> 01:40:11.290
People, you need to stop sinning.

550
01:40:11.290 --> 01:40:14.290
People, you need to lay down your stubbornness.

551
01:40:14.290 --> 01:40:17.290
People, let us carry this congregation together.

552
01:40:17.290 --> 01:40:19.290
Let us commit ourselves together.

553
01:40:19.290 --> 01:40:22.290
One of the problems of the people in the congregation...

554
01:40:22.290 --> 01:40:26.290
is sometimes that those people who do not participate...

555
01:40:26.290 --> 01:40:29.290
who are indeed stubborn, who do sin...

556
01:40:29.290 --> 01:40:33.290
and somehow still come on Sunday morning...

557
01:40:33.290 --> 01:40:36.290
commands like why you come, but well...

558
01:40:36.290 --> 01:40:40.290
and then still come, actually not much surrounded...

559
01:40:40.290 --> 01:40:43.290
Those people, when you address them about their behavior...

560
01:40:43.290 --> 01:40:46.290
do not receive it, because their heart is closed.

561
01:40:46.290 --> 01:40:48.290
Do you understand the concept I am saying?

562
01:40:48.290 --> 01:40:51.290
In one way or another, you can then tell those people...

563
01:40:51.290 --> 01:40:54.290
Stop that, stop that. No, go to the Lord.

564
01:40:54.290 --> 01:40:58.290
And that heart is closed. And that is frustrating, boy.

565
01:41:01.290 --> 01:41:06.290
And at that moment, you especially should not say to that person...

566
01:41:06.290 --> 01:41:09.290
It's going to be alright, you know. The Lord loves you. He is gracious.

567
01:41:10.290 --> 01:41:12.290
Such a verse...

568
01:41:14.290 --> 01:41:16.290
Yes, that can get to me...

569
01:41:16.290 --> 01:41:18.290
Where is that verse again?

570
01:41:18.290 --> 01:41:20.290
No, no, no.

571
01:41:20.290 --> 01:41:23.290
That can get to me... Only God can judge me.

572
01:41:23.290 --> 01:41:26.290
That is the text. Only God can judge me.

573
01:41:26.290 --> 01:41:28.290
Only God can judge me.

574
01:41:28.290 --> 01:41:31.290
Do you know what you are saying? God will judge you.

575
01:41:31.290 --> 01:41:33.290
That is the point.

576
01:41:33.290 --> 01:41:36.290
I mean, if the neighbor judges you, who cares?

577
01:41:37.290 --> 01:41:40.290
But if God judges you, that is very serious.

578
01:41:40.290 --> 01:41:42.290
And...

579
01:41:42.290 --> 01:41:45.290
Paul is dealing with...

580
01:41:45.290 --> 01:41:50.290
And I need to beautifully throw out the word balance.

581
01:41:50.290 --> 01:41:53.290
For we are not talking about balance here.

582
01:41:53.290 --> 01:41:55.290
We are not talking about...

583
01:41:55.290 --> 01:41:57.290
You must live a balanced life with God.

584
01:41:57.290 --> 01:42:02.290
A little grace and a little knowing that you will never be perfect.

585
01:42:02.290 --> 01:42:05.290
That is not the goal of what we are.

586
01:42:05.290 --> 01:42:09.290
The goal is that we come to know more of Him.

587
01:42:09.290 --> 01:42:12.290
So that we will love Him more.

588
01:42:12.290 --> 01:42:15.290
So that we will live as He is.

589
01:42:15.290 --> 01:42:17.290
That is the goal.

590
01:42:17.290 --> 01:42:19.290
We will read it together.

591
01:42:19.290 --> 01:42:22.290
Philippians chapter 3, verse 1.

592
01:42:25.290 --> 01:42:27.290
Philippians chapter 3, verse 1 says...

593
01:42:27.290 --> 01:42:31.290
But whatever happens, brothers and sisters, rejoice in the Lord.

594
01:42:32.290 --> 01:42:35.290
Can I get an amen from those who are happy?

595
01:42:35.290 --> 01:42:38.290
Seriously, here is a question.

596
01:42:38.290 --> 01:42:40.290
Here is a serious question.

597
01:42:40.290 --> 01:42:42.290
Are you happy in the Lord?

598
01:42:42.290 --> 01:42:45.290
Can I see a hand from those who are happy in the Lord?

599
01:42:45.290 --> 01:42:47.290
Nice.

600
01:42:47.290 --> 01:42:49.290
Nice.

601
01:42:49.290 --> 01:42:51.290
Christian, why are you happy in the Lord?

602
01:42:51.290 --> 01:42:53.290
Call it out once.

603
01:42:55.290 --> 01:42:57.290
He has forgiven you of your sin.

604
01:42:57.290 --> 01:42:59.290
And I see that joy in you.

605
01:42:59.290 --> 01:43:02.290
During the worship, I look through the room.

606
01:43:02.290 --> 01:43:05.290
I look to see who is not here today, I will then text them.

607
01:43:05.290 --> 01:43:08.290
But I saw you and I see the joy on your face.

608
01:43:08.290 --> 01:43:10.290
Joris, why are you happy?

609
01:43:12.290 --> 01:43:14.290
Yes, He has saved us, right?

610
01:43:14.290 --> 01:43:17.290
Henk Vermeulen, why are you happy?

611
01:43:19.290 --> 01:43:21.290
We have eternal life.

612
01:43:21.290 --> 01:43:23.290
I am also happy with you, Henk.

613
01:43:29.290 --> 01:43:33.290
Whatever happens, brothers and sisters, be happy.

614
01:43:33.290 --> 01:43:35.290
This is a command.

615
01:43:35.290 --> 01:43:39.290
Being happy is a command.

616
01:43:39.290 --> 01:43:42.290
Being happy is a law of God.

617
01:43:42.290 --> 01:43:44.290
You must be happy.

618
01:43:44.290 --> 01:43:46.290
You must be obliged to be happy.

619
01:43:46.290 --> 01:43:48.290
That's strange, isn't it?

620
01:43:48.290 --> 01:43:50.290
Paul says here, be happy.

621
01:43:50.290 --> 01:43:52.290
As a command to the congregation.

622
01:43:52.290 --> 01:43:58.290
For a number of things are not emotions that just happen to you.

623
01:43:59.290 --> 01:44:02.290
And that it is for one and not for the other.

624
01:44:02.290 --> 01:44:05.290
Faith is a choice.

625
01:44:05.290 --> 01:44:07.290
Love is a choice.

626
01:44:07.290 --> 01:44:10.290
And joy is a choice.

627
01:44:10.290 --> 01:44:14.290
You can choose to walk around being grumpy in life.

628
01:44:14.290 --> 01:44:21.290
And you can also choose to be happy with life in the Lord Jesus.

629
01:44:21.290 --> 01:44:27.290
And I see people in this church who are happy, glorifying the Lord...

630
01:44:27.290 --> 01:44:31.290
while they are going through valleys of what have you done to me.

631
01:44:31.290 --> 01:44:34.290
And then I think to myself, you know why?

632
01:44:34.290 --> 01:44:36.290
Because those people know God's Word.

633
01:44:36.290 --> 01:44:41.290
And they know in what position I find myself in life.

634
01:44:41.290 --> 01:44:43.290
I choose to be happy.

635
01:44:43.290 --> 01:44:48.290
For the joy of the Lord is your strength. Amen.

636
01:44:48.290 --> 01:44:50.290
That is such a cool Bible verse, right?

637
01:44:50.290 --> 01:44:52.290
I find it so cool to push it in there.

638
01:44:52.290 --> 01:44:54.290
That is such an awesome Bible verse.

639
01:44:54.290 --> 01:44:58.290
The joy of the Lord is your strength. Amen.

640
01:44:58.290 --> 01:45:02.290
Dear Nanny, may I take a look at that photo on the projector?

641
01:45:02.290 --> 01:45:03.290
There is indeed a book.

642
01:45:03.290 --> 01:45:09.290
And I will not often offer a book from the podium to people.

643
01:45:09.290 --> 01:45:13.290
But if you can listen in English, I don't think there is a Dutch translation of it.

644
01:45:13.290 --> 01:45:19.290
If you want to learn to be joyful in Christ, then buy this book.

645
01:45:19.290 --> 01:45:26.290
I bought this book years ago, in 2008, in an audio version.

646
01:45:26.290 --> 01:45:28.290
Back then it was still the time of CDs.

647
01:45:28.290 --> 01:45:31.290
I listened to it entirely on CDs.

648
01:45:31.290 --> 01:45:35.290
And this book has been a transformation for my life.

649
01:45:35.290 --> 01:45:39.290
John Piper, one of the best Bible teachers in this world.

650
01:45:39.290 --> 01:45:42.290
John Piper is truly a Paul figure.

651
01:45:42.290 --> 01:45:45.290
So thorough in the Word, so good, so stable, so safe.

652
01:45:45.290 --> 01:45:48.290
For do not read everything, for some things are dangerous.

653
01:45:48.290 --> 01:45:52.290
But John Piper has safe theology, you can learn from that.

654
01:45:52.290 --> 01:46:01.290
And in Desiring God, John Piper explains that it is a calling for a Christian to be joyful and to enjoy this life.

655
01:46:01.290 --> 01:46:05.290
Enjoying life is a command from the Lord.

656
01:46:05.290 --> 01:46:11.290
For if you start to grumble, you do not have the capacity in your soul to make Him great.

657
01:46:11.290 --> 01:46:15.290
But we must make Him great, for He is wonderful.

658
01:46:15.290 --> 01:46:24.290
But grumbling always has that skill to be amidst sunshine, amidst a full refrigerator, amidst a great time.

659
01:46:24.290 --> 01:46:26.290
I don't know, but I have to eat.

660
01:46:26.290 --> 01:46:29.290
And it is too warm, or it is too cold, or it is this.

661
01:46:29.290 --> 01:46:35.290
And sometimes I look at the grumpiness in life and think to myself, is that creative boy.

662
01:46:35.290 --> 01:46:38.290
Yes, but that is really true.

663
01:46:38.290 --> 01:46:43.290
But when you are grumpy, you cannot possibly magnify God.

664
01:46:43.290 --> 01:46:47.290
For God has given us so much, dear people.

665
01:46:47.290 --> 01:46:50.290
He has given us so much.

666
01:46:50.290 --> 01:46:52.290
We have it so good.

667
01:46:52.290 --> 01:46:56.290
We all have multiple pieces of clothing hanging in our closet.

668
01:46:56.290 --> 01:47:01.290
We all have multiple menus for this week in our refrigerator.

669
01:47:01.290 --> 01:47:07.290
We even have so much in the supermarket that we sometimes just get decision fatigue.

670
01:47:07.290 --> 01:47:09.290
Like, where shall I lie down tonight?

671
01:47:09.290 --> 01:47:12.290
Because there are probably 50,000 products there.

672
01:47:12.290 --> 01:47:16.290
It's insane how many reasons we have to magnify God.

673
01:47:16.290 --> 01:47:19.290
Be joyful and sing for the Lord.

674
01:47:19.290 --> 01:47:21.290
Exalt His name.

675
01:47:21.290 --> 01:47:23.290
Thank you for provision.

676
01:47:23.290 --> 01:47:25.290
Be glad that Jesus is here.

677
01:47:25.290 --> 01:47:27.290
Let us be a joyful church.

678
01:47:27.290 --> 01:47:29.290
Be glad, for He is good.

679
01:47:29.290 --> 01:47:31.290
He is so good.

680
01:47:31.290 --> 01:47:34.290
And that joy is a command.

681
01:47:34.290 --> 01:47:38.290
And what Paul says here, and now we are going to read a bit further, otherwise we will still be here at four o'clock.

682
01:47:38.290 --> 01:47:44.290
But whatever happens, brothers and sisters, rejoice in the Lord.

683
01:47:44.290 --> 01:47:49.290
For me, it is not at all bothersome, says Paul, to impose this as a law.

684
01:47:49.290 --> 01:47:53.290
For me, it is not at all bothersome to say this to you again.

685
01:47:53.290 --> 01:47:57.290
For we all need a kind of power of repetition.

686
01:47:57.290 --> 01:47:59.290
Sometimes you need this. Rejoice.

687
01:47:59.290 --> 01:48:01.290
Yes but yes, no, no, no. Rejoice.

688
01:48:01.290 --> 01:48:04.290
Yes but listen, no, no, no.

689
01:48:04.290 --> 01:48:06.290
Rejoice.

690
01:48:06.290 --> 01:48:12.290
And sometimes this zooming out is a warning for you.

691
01:48:12.290 --> 01:48:16.290
And you tend to voice a complaint from your flesh.

692
01:48:16.290 --> 01:48:19.290
Be still. Be still.

693
01:48:19.290 --> 01:48:22.290
And know that I am God, says the Lord.

694
01:48:22.290 --> 01:48:24.290
Yes but yes.

695
01:48:24.290 --> 01:48:26.290
I love you.

696
01:48:26.290 --> 01:48:28.290
Rejoice. Amen.

697
01:48:28.290 --> 01:48:32.290
For me, it is not at all bothersome to write this again.

698
01:48:32.290 --> 01:48:36.290
And for you, it is good to hear it once more.

699
01:48:36.290 --> 01:48:39.290
Does anyone here need to hear this sometimes, that you should rejoice?

700
01:48:39.290 --> 01:48:42.290
I do, even though I am an optimist.

701
01:48:42.290 --> 01:48:46.290
But I just know joy. The joy of the Lord is my strength.

702
01:48:46.290 --> 01:48:48.290
I need to be here regularly.

703
01:48:48.290 --> 01:48:52.290
No matter what the world can do, no matter what can happen, I am glad.

704
01:48:52.290 --> 01:48:55.290
Because I have a Lord God. Hallelujah.

705
01:48:55.290 --> 01:49:01.290
Verse 2. And now we come to the thesis of what Paul is doing here in this powerful chapter.

706
01:49:01.290 --> 01:49:02.290
Verse 2.

707
01:49:02.290 --> 01:49:09.290
Beware of the people who do not truly serve the Lord.

708
01:49:09.290 --> 01:49:13.290
They harm you with their wrong ideas.

709
01:49:13.290 --> 01:49:20.290
For they want you to be circumcised because they think you do not belong to God otherwise.

710
01:49:20.290 --> 01:49:26.290
But it is completely pointless to be circumcised.

711
01:49:26.290 --> 01:49:30.290
Rachel, may I please borrow your Bible for a moment?

712
01:49:30.290 --> 01:49:36.290
So we can show how the basic Bible is far too gentle for the Dutch.

713
01:49:36.290 --> 01:49:43.290
Because the basic Bible says, beware of the people who do not truly serve the Lord.

714
01:49:43.290 --> 01:49:47.290
Listen to what Paul says in English.

715
01:49:56.290 --> 01:49:59.290
Mutilators of the flesh.

716
01:49:59.290 --> 01:50:06.290
Dogs, evil doers and mutilators of the flesh.

717
01:50:06.290 --> 01:50:10.290
The Bible scolds in a few places.

718
01:50:10.290 --> 01:50:12.290
And this is one of them.

719
01:50:12.290 --> 01:50:14.290
John once scolded well.

720
01:50:14.290 --> 01:50:16.290
Jesus once scolded.

721
01:50:16.290 --> 01:50:18.290
And Paul does it here too.

722
01:50:18.290 --> 01:50:20.290
John says, you brood of vipers.

723
01:50:20.290 --> 01:50:25.290
Jesus says, you are whitewashed tombs.

724
01:50:25.290 --> 01:50:27.290
It is peculiar.

725
01:50:27.290 --> 01:50:31.290
And here it says, beware of those dogs.

726
01:50:31.290 --> 01:50:34.290
For Paul is angry about what we are about to read.

727
01:50:34.290 --> 01:50:37.290
Yes, there is one enthusiastic.

728
01:50:37.290 --> 01:50:39.290
I love my mom, for she is so into the Word.

729
01:50:39.290 --> 01:50:42.290
And indeed, his lifestyle.

730
01:50:42.290 --> 01:50:44.290
Love it. Pay attention.

731
01:50:44.290 --> 01:50:47.290
So we will read it one more time.

732
01:50:47.290 --> 01:50:53.290
Beware of those dogs, who do not really serve the Lord.

733
01:50:53.290 --> 01:50:55.290
And Paul is getting angry in his words.

734
01:50:55.290 --> 01:51:00.290
Paul, you see a righteous anger rising up in him.

735
01:51:00.290 --> 01:51:06.290
For he says, those people want you to be circumcised.

736
01:51:06.290 --> 01:51:10.290
And whether you want to be circumcised for hygiene, or I don't know what.

737
01:51:10.290 --> 01:51:12.290
You have to decide that for yourself.

738
01:51:12.290 --> 01:51:15.290
In North America and Australia, many boys.

739
01:51:15.290 --> 01:51:18.290
The large part of society is still being circumcised.

740
01:51:18.290 --> 01:51:21.290
It is not only exclusive to Muslims and Jews.

741
01:51:21.290 --> 01:51:25.290
You can choose to be circumcised for any reason you like.

742
01:51:25.290 --> 01:51:28.290
But what is central here is important.

743
01:51:28.290 --> 01:51:30.290
And that should provoke anger.

744
01:51:30.290 --> 01:51:36.290
For they want you to be circumcised because they believe that otherwise you do not belong to God.

745
01:51:36.290 --> 01:51:39.290
And this provokes anger in Paul.

746
01:51:39.290 --> 01:51:44.290
For Paul says, it is completely pointless to be circumcised.

747
01:51:44.290 --> 01:51:48.290
For it does not help us if we cut into our bodies.

748
01:51:48.290 --> 01:51:52.290
We are truly circumcised and therefore truly belong to God.

749
01:51:52.290 --> 01:51:55.290
When we serve God, through His Spirit.

750
01:51:55.290 --> 01:51:57.290
And when we trust in whom?

751
01:51:57.290 --> 01:51:59.290
In Jesus Christ.

752
01:51:59.290 --> 01:52:00.290
To be saved.

753
01:52:00.290 --> 01:52:02.290
And not in ourselves.

754
01:52:02.290 --> 01:52:04.290
And Paul has a revelation here.

755
01:52:04.290 --> 01:52:07.290
He thinks, Jesus hung naked on a cross.

756
01:52:07.290 --> 01:52:09.290
They mutilated him.

757
01:52:09.290 --> 01:52:10.290
They caused him pain.

758
01:52:10.290 --> 01:52:13.290
He was God Himself, as we read in the previous chapter.

